```python
def countSpecialCharacters(word: str) -> int:
    # Use sets to store lowercase and uppercase characters present in the word
    lower_chars = set()
    upper_chars = set()

    for char in word:
        if char.islower():
            lower_chars.add(char)
        elif char.isupper():
            upper_chars.add(char.lower())

    # The intersection of both sets gives characters that appear in both cases
    special_letters = lower_chars.intersection(upper_chars)

    return len(special_letters)
```

